 "text": "Hi, how have you been? First, sorry, that's a stressful thing to be late for. No, walk in as soon as the room is free and the couple are alone. The groom's best man will usually tell you when. Only if you know them well and can text without being weird. Otherwise, wait until you see them face to face. Try leaving early and parking a bit away. Many venues have a shuttle, and you' save an anxious walk. Weddings are usually well prepared for last minute problems, so don't stress too much. Just be friendly and polite.",
